text:
zoe: Noting a slightly different leak case in the Go generator sample: when auth refresh triggers inside the transport we briefly replace the http.Client, and any recv goroutines holding the old client hang. Observed in local e2e when I force a delayed refresh.

marc: hmm, that's nasty. Can you paste the simplified pattern?

zoe: minimal repro from sample app:
```go
func streamHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
  ctx := r.Context()
  s, _ := client.Generator.OpenStream(ctx, opts)
  defer s.Close()

  // spawn worker to push to SSE
  go func() {
    for {
      msg, err := s.Recv()
      if err != nil { return }
      // write SSE
    }
  }()

  // keep handler alive until ctx.Done or stream ends
  <-ctx.Done()
}
```
\nashley: even with defer Close, if the transport swaps mid-Recv the old Recv can block on read because its internal ctx was backgrounded. We should ensure: (1) transport operations accept a parent ctx; (2) OpenStream ties all internals to caller ctx or exposes a Close that cancels those internals.

marc: API idea: StreamHandle that exposes Done() chan, Close() cancels everything, and an OpenUntilReady(ctx, opts) variant that waits for auth to settle. Example:
```go
h, err := client.Generator.OpenUntilReady(ctx, opts)
if err != nil { /* handle */ }
defer h.Close()
select {
case m := <-h.Messages():
  // handle
case <-h.Done():
  return h.Err()
case <-ctx.Done():
  h.Close()
  return ctx.Err()
}
```

zoe: OpenUntilReady is nice: avoids first-message 401s when onboarding sample hits a slow KMS. Also: implement small retry policy for transient 401s on idempotent streams (with capped backoff) and log retries at debug level so users can diagnose.

ashley: small ergonomics ask: provide a convenience helper that returns a channel and a cleanup func to close it. Many users prefer channel-based loops in examples. Something like: msgs, closeFn := client.Generator.StreamAsChannel(ctx, opts) 
// defer closeFn()

marc: agree but avoid too many variants. Let's standardize on OpenStream/OpenUntilReady names and add StreamAsChannel as a thin wrapper in devex examples. We'll deprecate Generator.Start in docs.

infra-bot: created issue DE-900: StreamHandle API + transport context propagation + retry policy. Assigned @marc.

zoe: I'll open a small PR with the StreamHandle interface, sampleapp update showing defer Close + goroutine count test, and a unit that cancels during a forced auth sleep to catch leaks.

marc: when you do, include a test that simulates replacing the underlying http.Client mid-stream to reproduce the blocking-read scenario. Also add docs note: "Always Close streams; use OpenUntilReady for slow auth backends."

ashley: last nit: add a one-line migration note for users: "If you used raw Generator.Start, switch to OpenStream and ensure defer Close to avoid background goroutine leaks and auth races."

zoe: will do. Thanks!
